Fetch a supported model artifact into the local cache

Usage: bitnet model fetch [OPTIONS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>  Supported model id, for example qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-q8_0

Options:
  -c, --config <PATH>      Configuration file path
      --cache-dir <PATH>   Override cache root. Defaults to ~/.cache/bitnet-rs/models
  -d, --device <DEVICE>    Device/backend label (cpu, cuda/gpu, hip/rocm, oneapi, npu/openvino-npu, nvidia-rtx-5070-ti-cuda/wgpu, intel-a770-opencl, metal/mpsgraph, apple-m4-metal, apple-m4-mpsgraph, apple-m4-cpu-neon, apple-m3-air-metal, apple-m3-air-mpsgraph, apple-m3-air-cpu-neon, auto). Apple M4 and M3 Air labels are distinct proof lanes
      --offline            Do not use the network; pass if an already verified artifact is cached
      --force              Re-download even when a verified artifact already exists
      --log-level <LEVEL>  Log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)
      --json               Emit JSON instead of text
      --threads <N>        Number of CPU threads
      --batch-size <SIZE>  Batch size for processing
  -h, --help               Print help
